codemap 9
tour feature-tour
kind flow
author ai
group features/cli
note tour <name> [--inline]: one tour as a document to read top to bottom instead of opening files. The agent reaches for it to read a mapped workflow as one document instead of opening every file its steps point into. It prints the tour's title and note, which other tours link to it, then every step in tree order with its note and its code as numbered lines. Steps are numbered like sections (1, 1.1, 1.2, 2) and a '-- back in <symbol> --' line marks the return to a shallower level, so a long flow reads like a book. With --inline, a step that links to another tour is followed by that tour's steps inline, numbered under the linking step; a tour already open higher up is not inlined again, which keeps a link cycle finite.

